Keeps this stage in git.

A card arrives here from 6-done and stays until production has been asked the four questions in
operate-after-done: what is erroring, what got slower, what did users do that we did not design
for, and what did it cost.

The board used to end at 6-done. Paying customers start there. Anything production says that
would change what gets built leaves here as a NEW card in 0-discovery, with the observation
pasted in — because an incident that produced no card will happen again identically.
